1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,620
Repeated API reads send the same request
back to the database,

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,270
adding avoidable time.

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,990
Even when the answer is unchanged,

4
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:13,420
each repeat adds delay and keeps the
database doing work again.

5
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,850
A cache keeps a copy near the API.

6
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,360
A miss fetches from the database
and fills the cache;

7
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:22,750
a hit returns that copy directly.

8
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,960
The answer stays the same;

9
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:29,510
repeat reads take a shorter route without
another database round trip.

10
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:32,700
Synthetic p95 latency:

11
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,080
420 ms before,

12
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:39,310
180 ms after — about 57% lower.

13
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,450
Set freshness rules.

14
00:00:41,610 --> 00:00:45,520
Measure your own workload before
promising any improvement.
